---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import '../styles/marketing.css';
---

<MarketingLayout>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="KitchooK! home">KitchooK<span>!</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a class="nav-link" href="/docs/introduction/quick-start/">Quick start</a>
      <a class="nav-link" href="/docs/introduction/">Docs</a>
      <a class="nav-link" href="https://demo.kitchook.com">Live demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <h1 id="hero-title">Clear out the recipe drawer.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Your cookbook goes <em>where you host it.</em></p>
      <p class="hero-description">KitchooK! turns Markdown recipes and photos into a fast, searchable static website you can host yourself.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/docs/introduction/quick-start/">Build your cookbook <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="https://demo.kitchook.com">See the live demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principles" aria-label="KitchooK! principles">
      <article>
        <p class="number">01</p>
        <h2>Your recipes are plain Markdown.</h2>
        <p>Your collection stays readable as plain text files with photos right alongside them. The files remain useful without KitchooK!.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="number">02</p>
        <h2>Build once. Host the files.</h2>
        <p>KitchooK! generates HTML, CSS, JavaScript, client-side search data, and a static JSON recipe export. Serve the result from a compatible static host.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="number">03</p>
        <h2>Your content stays yours.</h2>
        <p>Keep your recipes in a private folder or repository. The build reads that folder without modifying your recipe files.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Simple 3-step workflow</p>
        <h2 id="workflow-title">From a recipe folder to a fast website.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Write</strong><span>Plain text and photos</span></li>
        <li><strong>Build</strong><span>Use Node.js or Docker</span></li>
        <li><strong>Host</strong><span>Copy files to a static host</span></li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link nav-link" href="/docs/introduction/how-it-works/">How static generation works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-callout" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Try it before you build it</p>
      <h2 id="demo-title">A working cookbook built from example recipes.</h2>
      <p>The demo is built from KitchooK!'s bundled examples using the normal source-build workflow.</p>
      <a class="button primary" href="https://demo.kitchook.com">Open demo.kitchook.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="KitchooK! home">KitchooK<span>!</span></a>
    <p>Markdown recipes, made portable.</p>
    <div><a class="nav-link" href="/docs/introduction/">Documentation</a><a class="nav-link" href="https://demo.kitchook.com">Live demo</a><a class="nav-link" href="https://github.com/Refueled/kitchook">Source</a><a class="nav-link" href="https://github.com/Refueled/kitchook/releases">Releases</a><a class="nav-link" href="/docs/project/contributing-and-security/">Security</a></div>
  </footer>
</MarketingLayout>
